start     book
terminals word

# The D'ni's own books (design §4.2), and the only place a modifier is taught. Every book here should use
# one where the Age it makes shows what it did (§4.5): an `except` should leave out something the world
# would otherwise have. BookCheck fails any book that uses no grammatical word but `age`.

book = <mingled_age> | <spared_age> | <thronged_age> | <sited_age>

# `and`: two stones laid together, so the rock visibly holds both.
mingled_age = <bleak_mood> age patchy <hot_stone> and <dark_stone> landmass molten sea
    | age patchy <cold_stone> and <pale_stone> landmass frozen climate

# `except`: the creatures a world would grow, less one a visitor would miss.
spared_age = age except <monster> spawns temperate climate

# A quantifier: one creature, far more often than the world would grow it.
thronged_age = age teeming <beast> spawns verdant biomes

# `in`: a feature confined to one biome. Torchflowers are the pack's own, so this is judged on a server.
sited_age = age torchflowers features in jungle

bleak_mood = desolate | ancient | foreboding

hot_stone = basalt | magma_block

dark_stone = blackstone | deepslate

cold_stone = packed_ice | blue_ice

pale_stone = snow_block | calcite

monster = zombie | skeleton | creeper

beast = sheep | rabbit | horse
